# SPARK — local development environment. Copy to `.env` and fill in.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# ⛔ `.env` IS GIT-IGNORED AND ONLY AFFECTS *LOCAL* BUILDS.
#
# The live site at spark-online.space is built by GitHub Actions from a clean checkout, which never
# sees this file. To make a relay reach the DEPLOYED game you must set the same three values as
# repository secrets — see TURN_SETUP.md. This file is for `npm run dev` / a local `npm run build`.

# ─── TURN relay (multiplayer across strict networks) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated. Both a udp and a tcp/443 url is the usual pairing — tcp/443 is what gets through
# restrictive corporate and hotel networks that block everything else.
VITE_TURN_URLS=turn:standard.relay.metered.ca:80,turn:standard.relay.metered.ca:443?transport=tcp
VITE_TURN_USERNAME=
VITE_TURN_CREDENTIAL=
